## Running Locally

Two terminals are required — one for the Python backend, one for the Next.js frontend.

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.11+ with dependencies installed (`pip install -r backend/requirements.txt`)
- Node.js 18+ with dependencies installed (`npm install`)
- `.env.local` at the project root with the following set:
  ```
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
  BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000
  OPENAI_API_KEY=<your key>
  ```

### Terminal 1 — Backend (FastAPI + Uvicorn)

> ⚠️ Must be run from the **project root** (`d:\chancellor\MRIIQ`), not from inside `backend/`.
> The module path `backend.app.main:app` requires the root on the Python path.

```powershell
cd d:\chancellor\MRIIQ
python -m uvicorn backend.app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

Backend will be available at: `http://localhost:8000`

### Terminal 2 — Frontend (Next.js)

```powershell
cd d:\chancellor\MRIIQ
npm run dev
```

Frontend will be available at: `http://localhost:3000`

